bilbo read: print an entry's outline, or its records a page at a time.

[1mUsage:[22m
  [36mbilbo read [39m[2m<ref>[22m[36m [--budget [39m[2m<tokens>[22m[36m][39m
  [36mbilbo read [39m[2m<ref>[22m[36m --outline [--budget [39m[2m<tokens>[22m[36m][39m
[2m<ref> is an entry id or a session id, then #r<a>-<b> for records a to b, #g<n>[22m
[2mfor an older generation, or #g<n>:r<a>-<b>.[22m

[1mOptions:[22m
      [1m--outline[22m          List the prompts or sections of the range, not its text
      [1m--budget [22m[2m<tokens>[22m  Print at most this many tokens a page

[1mOutput:[22m
  [1m#r[22m[2m<n>[22m[1m [22m[2m<label>[22m[1m: [22m[2m<text>[22m  each record after its locator, as it was kept
  [1mmore: bilbo read ...[22m   the last line: the command for the next page
  [1mend: ...[22m               the last line: nothing is left of what was asked
  [1mcut: ...; more: ...[22m    the last line after a cut record: how to read it whole
[2mWith no #r: metadata and outline. Only the last line is bilbo's own.[22m

[1mExit:[22m
  [1m0[22m  success, also when no record of the range renders
  [1m1[22m  no such entry, a range outside it, or no store
  [1m2[22m  usage or config error, or a session id that names several entries

[1mExamples:[22m
  [36mbilbo read 01M6ZGE4KTBYYH07AS2KVMSCAF[39m
  [36mbilbo read 01M6ZGE4KTBYYH07AS2KVMSCAF#r120-184[39m
  [36mbilbo read 2d6b1857 --outline[39m

[1mDocs:[22m [2mhttps://github.com/delucca/bilbo/wiki/Commands#read[22m
